      "likelyResponse": "Focus is a function of clarity and urgency. If you’re losing focus, it’s likely because the task isn’t clearly defined or doesn’t feel urgent enough. Break big problems into tiny, time-boxed actions. Work in 90-minute sprints with zero distractions—phone off, notifications off. If it’s not important enough to warrant that level of intensity, question whether it’s worth doing at all.",
      "followUpQuestions": [
        "What specifically are you trying to accomplish?",
        "Have you broken your goal into the smallest possible next actions?",
        "Are you measuring progress daily?"
      ],
      "suggestedAction": "Define your top 3 critical tasks for the week. Schedule 90-minute deep work blocks for each in your calendar. Eliminate all non-essential meetings and notifications during those blocks."
